# K03 NS-ROLES-3: the exact-actual twin of unit_walk_a3_capture_direct_vs_copy (walked).  The host is passed the named Structure Model
# itself -- a value exactly of its formal's model -- so the capture is admitted as itself (the pins); the migrated
# row passes a merge result, admitted by name.  A3 (Codex, 2026-09-28): the direct calls pass the host's current
# values -- m by reference, so read's write `m\other` is the root's Model -- and the node the host's return builds
# carries its own copies, which later writes of Model do not reach and read's writes do not leave.  seen_a 41,
# seen_b 1141, Model\other 5 -> 7, then 7000 and the node reads 1141 twice.  Success is 7; else 64 plus a bit.
Model:
    int: value 0
    int: other 5
    int: seen_a 0
    int: seen_b 0
end: Model

fn: makeReader (Model: m; int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: read (int: x) int
        m\other: m\other + 1
        return: m\value + n + x
    m\seen_a: (read: 0)
    m\value: m\value + 100
    n: n + 1000
    m\seen_b: (read: 0)
    return: read

Model\value: 40
@: r makeReader(Model; 1)
int: sa 0
int: sb 0
int: o1 0
sa: Model\seen_a
sb: Model\seen_b
o1: Model\other
Model\value: 7000
Model\other: 7000
int: c (r: 0)
int: d (r: 0)
int: o2 0
o2: Model\other
int: bad 0
if: sa != 41
    bad: bad + 1
if: sb != 1141
    bad: bad + 2
if: o1 != 7
    bad: bad + 4
if: c != 1141
    bad: bad + 8
if: d != 1141
    bad: bad + 16
if: o2 != 7000
    bad: bad + 32
int: ok 7
if: bad != 0
    ok: 64 + bad
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
